+## 8. Replay set (round 11 — build_replay_set.py)
+
+Built with `python3 bench/build_replay_set.py` (r10 run, exit 0, read-only; no GPU).
+
+**Outputs** (gitignored, recorded content; only the manifest is committed):
+- `bench/.replay/m1/agent.jsonl` — one line per recorded agent LLM request (assistant turn).
+- `bench/.replay/m1/mem.jsonl` — one line per rebuilt mem0 extraction call.
+- `bench/results/2026-10-12/m1-ngram/replay_manifest.json` — committed, no request content.
+
+**Sizes / distinct steps**
+- agent: 30 requests across 6 distinct steps — `baseline-r0/0`, `baseline-r1/0`,
+  `baseline-r1/2`, `mem0-r0/0`, `mem0-r1/0`, `mem0-r2/0`. Both arms (3 baseline
+  steps + 3 mem0 steps); steps chosen for file reads, edits and test output
+  (`step_score`). 60 agent turns were available in the top steps; 5 kept per step.
+- mem: 12 requests across 5 distinct steps — `mem0-r0/0`, `mem0-r0/1`, `mem0-r0/2`,
+  `mem0-r1/0`, `mem0-r1/1`. (mem0-r2 steps had no mem tap records.) One request
+  per `mem` tap record, in per-call order (tool-add vs auto-capture, §7 and the
+  round 8–10 notes).
+
+**est/recorded ratios** (chars/4 divided by `(prompt_n+cache_n)`, the recorded tap
+token count; `recorded_prompt_tokens` present on every entry):
+- agent median **0.833** (in range 0.75–1.33); mem median **1.027** (in range).
+- agent `n_messages<=3` ratios: `[0.846, 0.846, 0.84, 0.877, 0.877, 0.877]` —
+  used as the sanity check that the agent system prompt + tool-scheme
+  reconstruction is exact (see `system_prompt_note` in the manifest; `getSystemMessageText`
+  is not in `pi_prompt_src.txt`, so the section join is INFERRED).
+
+**Outliers** (ratio outside 0.75–1.33): 3, all later turns of the longest
+baseline session `baseline-r0/0`, none elsewhere: 0/5 (0.740), 0/8 (0.743),
+0/10 (0.742). Explanation — these are cumulative, reasoning-heavy turns.
+`chars_by_role` for each (system 2583, tools 2841, user 763 are per-turn
+constants; the variance is reasoning + tool + assistant):
+
+| id            | ratio | reasoning | tool | assistant | total chars | recorded tokens | chars/token |
+|---------------|-------|-----------|------|-----------|-------------|-----------------|-------------|
+| baseline-r0/0/5   | 0.740 | 25717 | 2156 | 4475 | 38533 | 13032 | 2.96 |
+| baseline-r0/0/8   | 0.743 | 26225 | 3444 | 5507 | 41363 | 13939 | 2.97 |
+| baseline-r0/0/10  | 0.742 | 26591 | 3753 | 5918 | 42449 | 14317 | 2.96 |
+
+The chars/4 estimator assumes 4 chars/token, but these turns tokenize at **~3.0
+chars/token** (tool output / file-read / test-output / JSON-heavy content
+tokenizes at <4 chars/token, as the advisor expected). That consistent ~29%
+under-estimate of tokens pushes the 3 ratios just below the 0.75 floor. No
+missing history is involved (n_messages mismatches = 0) and the median (0.833)
+is comfortably in range — the floor is only crossed by these individual tool-heavy
+turns, so the ratio criterion is met and the replay set is sound.
+
+**Note on the 3-way agent ratio check (r10):** the "reasoning after last user
+only" ratio equals the "all reasoning" ratio for *every* step (both 0.833
+medians). This is not template evidence — each replayed step is a fresh session
+whose first message is the single user prompt, so all assistant turns follow it.
+The meaningful check is that the "no reasoning" median is 0.457 (below range),
+which is why `reasoning_content` must be kept in agent bodies (see standing
+fact: recorded agent prompts included earlier reasoning, e.g. baseline-r0/0
+prompt grows 2761 to 13032 tokens by turn 5).
